{"ld": 1970, "paper": "HP1314", "session": "132", "title": "An Act to Amend the Laws Regarding Consent for HIV Testing and Disclosure of Related Medical Information for Insurance Purposes", "sponsor_id": "h-osher-laurie", "cosponsor_ids": ["s-brenner-stacy", "h-eder-john", "h-fecteau-ryan", "h-flynn-paul", "h-mathieson-kristi", "h-moonen-matthew", "h-rana-ambureen", "h-roeder-amy", "h-supica-laura"], "committee_code": "HCIFS", "committee_name": "Health Coverage, Insurance and Financial Services", "summary": {"text": "This bill provides that an HIV test may be undertaken with a patient's general consent. The bill defines \"general consent\" to mean consent obtained without undue inducement or any element of compulsion, fraud, deceit, duress or any other form of constraint or coercion and that is obtained after providing instruction to a patient that, as part of a medical procedure or test, the patient may receive an HIV test and that receiving an HIV test is voluntary and the patient may choose not to submit to an HIV test. The bill also provides that disclosure of information in a medical record for the purpose of seeking insurance reimbursement for HIV testing is not precluded. The bill removes the requirement that an HIV test may be undertaken only with a patient's informed consent.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP1314&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "enacted", "status_label": "Enacted", "final_disposition": {"label": "Enacted", "date": "2026-03-19", "governor_action": "Signed", "governor_action_date": "2026-03-19"}, "fiscal_status": "No Fiscal Impact", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 1970)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP1314&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (H-541)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP1314&item=2&snum=132", "item": 2}, {"label": "Amendment C-B (H-801)", "url": "https://legislatu